const PRIVACY = "## Introduction\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how S.R.L. PROMSTAR SERVICE (\"Company,\" \"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\") handles information in connection with GTL｜Getting Out (the \"Application\" or \"App\").\n\nS.R.L. PROMSTAR SERVICE is a limited liability company established under the laws of the Republic of Moldova.\n\nRegistered Address: Republic of Moldova, Chisinau Municipality, Ciocana Sector, 116/10 Ismail Street, Apt./Off. 2.\n\nContact Email: coj@promstarservice.store\n\nWe recognize the importance of protecting user information and aim to maintain transparent practices concerning the collection, use, processing, and protection of information associated with the Application.\n\nBy accessing or using the Application, you acknowledge the data practices described in this Privacy Policy.\n\n## Application Services\n\nThe Application provides tools designed to assist users in finding correctional facility information, locating supported inmate profiles, organizing contact details, and accessing available communication features.\n\nThe Application may also offer an AI-powered assistant that helps users prepare messages, express thoughts, and find suitable wording when communicating with incarcerated individuals.\n\nCertain communication features require an active subscription.\n\nThe information processed depends on the features selected and the services used.\n\n## Information We Process\n\nDepending on your interactions with the Application, the following categories of information may be processed:\n\n### Communication Information\n\nMessages and other text entered into communication features may be processed to provide the requested functionality.\n\n### Search Information\n\nSearch terms, selected facility details, and information provided when searching for inmate profiles may be used to display relevant results.\n\n### Saved Profiles and Contacts\n\nInformation that users choose to save, including selected profiles, search results, and contact details, may be maintained locally on their devices.\n\n### AI Assistant Inputs\n\nText submitted to the AI assistant is processed to generate writing suggestions, supportive responses, or communication guidance.\n\n### Subscription Information\n\nSubscription status, transaction identifiers, purchased product information, and related technical identifiers may be processed to verify subscription access.\n\n### Technical Information\n\nLimited device-related or application-related information may be processed when necessary for subscription verification, service operation, and technical functionality.\n\nThe Application does not require users to provide unnecessary personal information to access features that do not depend on it.\n\n## AI Assistant and Data Processing\n\nThe Application includes an AI-powered assistant that provides automated assistance with writing and communication.\n\nThe assistant may help users:\n\n- Draft personal messages.\n- Improve or rephrase existing text.\n- Find supportive or encouraging expressions.\n- Communicate thoughts during emotionally challenging situations.\n- Generate suggestions for maintaining meaningful communication.\n\nTo provide these features, text submitted by users is transmitted to a third-party AI service for processing.\n\nThe Application does not maintain a persistent history of AI conversations. User prompts and generated responses are not intentionally retained by the Application after the interaction is completed.\n\nHowever, the external AI service provider may process or retain information according to its applicable privacy practices, technical requirements, and legal obligations.\n\nUsers are encouraged not to enter highly sensitive personal information, financial details, passwords, identification numbers, or confidential information about themselves or other individuals.\n\nAI-generated responses are provided for informational and communication assistance purposes. They may contain errors or unsuitable suggestions and should be reviewed before use.\n\n## Messaging and Communication Features\n\nThe Application may provide access to messaging functionality associated with supported correctional communication services.\n\nInformation submitted through these features may be processed by the communication systems responsible for delivering or handling messages.\n\nCorrectional facilities and communication providers may apply their own policies concerning message screening, monitoring, delivery, retention, and availability.\n\nWe cannot guarantee that messages transmitted through external communication systems will remain private or confidential.\n\nUsers should review the applicable communication rules before submitting personal or sensitive information.\n\n## Local Information Storage\n\nCertain Application information may be stored directly on the user's device, including saved profiles, contact references, selected search results, and application preferences.\n\nLocal storage allows users to access selected information more conveniently.\n\nThe Application does not maintain a permanent AI conversation history.\n\nInformation stored locally may be removed through available Application controls or by uninstalling the Application, subject to operating system backup and restoration behavior.\n\n## Subscription Services\n\nThe Application uses Apphud, a third-party subscription management service, to support subscription functionality.\n\nApphud may process information necessary to manage subscription access, including:\n\n- Subscription status.\n- Product identifiers.\n- Purchase and renewal information.\n- Transaction identifiers.\n- Automatically generated user or device-related identifiers.\n- Limited technical information required for subscription management.\n\nPayments are processed through Apple's App Store payment infrastructure.\n\nWe do not receive or store complete payment card information.\n\nSubscription-related information is handled according to the applicable privacy practices of Apple and Apphud.\n\n## How Information Is Used\n\nInformation may be processed for the following purposes:\n\n- Providing Application features and requested services.\n- Supporting inmate and correctional facility searches.\n- Enabling available communication functionality.\n- Generating responses through the AI assistant.\n- Maintaining locally saved information.\n- Verifying purchases and subscription entitlements.\n- Restoring previously purchased subscriptions.\n- Responding to user inquiries.\n- Maintaining security and preventing misuse.\n- Complying with applicable legal obligations.\n\nWhere required by applicable law, processing is carried out on an appropriate legal basis, such as performance of a service requested by the user, legitimate operational interests, compliance with legal requirements, or consent.\n\n## Third-Party Services\n\nCertain Application functions depend on services provided by independent third parties.\n\nThese may include:\n\n### Apple\n\nApple processes App Store purchases, subscription billing, and related transactions.\n\n### Apphud\n\nApphud provides subscription management and entitlement verification services.\n\n### AI Service Providers\n\nExternal AI technology providers process submitted text to generate automated responses and writing suggestions.\n\n### Communication and Information Services\n\nSupported external systems may provide facility information, search results, or communication functionality.\n\nInformation shared with these providers is subject to their respective privacy practices and applicable legal requirements.\n\nWe do not control the independent data handling procedures of external providers.\n\n## Brand Authorization and Application Operation\n\nS.R.L. PROMSTAR SERVICE operates the Application under a signed Brand Name and Trademark Authorization Agreement, effective October 22, 2026, with Global Tel*Link Corporation, doing business as ViaPath Technologies.\n\nUnder this agreement, S.R.L. PROMSTAR SERVICE is authorized to use the GettingOut name and approved brand elements in connection with the development, publication, distribution, operation, maintenance, and support of the Application.\n\nThis authorization concerns the permitted use of the GettingOut brand and related intellectual property.\n\nS.R.L. PROMSTAR SERVICE remains responsible for operating the Application and handling information processed through its features.\n\nThe brand authorization does not independently establish access rights to correctional facility systems, proprietary communication infrastructure, or restricted information.\n\nThe Application is not a government-operated service, and the brand authorization does not imply endorsement by any correctional institution or public authority.\n\n## Data Retention\n\nInformation is retained only to the extent necessary for legitimate operational purposes, subscription management, legal compliance, security, or the provision of requested features.\n\nAI conversation history is not intentionally stored by the Application.\n\nInformation submitted to external AI services may be subject to the retention practices of the relevant provider.\n\nSubscription records may be maintained by Apple and Apphud according to their respective policies and legal requirements.\n\nLocally stored information generally remains on the user's device until removed or otherwise affected by device settings and application management.\n\n## Information Security\n\nWe take reasonable measures intended to protect information handled through the Application against unauthorized access, misuse, loss, or alteration.\n\nNevertheless, no electronic system or data transmission method can guarantee absolute security.\n\nUsers are responsible for maintaining appropriate security measures for their devices and accounts.\n\nWe encourage users to avoid sharing confidential information unless necessary for the requested functionality.\n\n## International Data Processing\n\nSome third-party technology providers may process information outside the country in which a user resides.\n\nWhere applicable, such processing is subject to relevant privacy requirements and the safeguards implemented by the responsible service providers.\n\nThe availability of particular rights and protections may vary depending on the user's jurisdiction.\n\n## Children's Privacy\n\nThe Application is not designed specifically for children.\n\nUsers must meet the minimum age requirements applicable to their location and the relevant App Store restrictions.\n\nWe do not knowingly process children's personal information in violation of applicable law.\n\nIf information concerning a child has been improperly submitted, a parent or legal guardian may contact us to request appropriate action.\n\n## User Rights and Choices\n\nDepending on applicable data protection laws, users may have rights concerning personal information associated with them.\n\nThese rights may include:\n\n- Requesting access to personal information.\n- Requesting correction of inaccurate information.\n- Requesting deletion of eligible information.\n- Objecting to or restricting certain processing activities.\n- Withdrawing consent where processing depends on consent.\n- Requesting information about the handling of personal data.\n\nRequests may be submitted using the contact information provided below.\n\nSome requests may require additional verification or may need to be directed to the relevant independent service provider.\n\n## Changes to This Privacy Policy\n\nWe may modify this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in Application functionality, legal obligations, technology providers, or information-handling practices.\n\nUpdated versions will be made available through the Application or another appropriate communication method.\n\nThe date at the beginning of this Policy indicates when the current version was last updated.\n\n## Contact Information\n\nFor questions, privacy inquiries, or requests concerning personal information, please contact:\n\n### S.R.L. PROMSTAR SERVICE\n\nRepublic of Moldova, Chisinau Municipality, Ciocana Sector, 116/10 Ismail Street, Apt./Off. 2\n\nEmail: coj@promstarservice.store";

